-- The Brauer group of a local field and symbols at the real places: the
-- class of an invariant b : ℚ/ℤ → H²(Γ, Ωˣ) of a henselian local field is
-- bijective and multiplies by the index under restriction; classes dying
-- on V are multiples of one such class; Kummer cocycles count
-- n²·#(O/n), and 1-cocycles of finite modules are finite; the local Artin
-- map sends uniformisers to geometric Frobenius elements; a character
-- killing every symbol is trivial; complex conjugations exist at real
-- places, are involutions, act by −1 through the cyclotomic characters,
-- do not exist over totally complex fields, and the symbol of a totally
-- positive element dies on an open subgroup containing them.
-- Source: grh-compact/src/Lib/ClassField/LocalDuality/RealPlaceSymbols.lean
-- (mem_zmultiples_of_resH2_eq_zero, isClassOfInv_classOfInv,
-- resH2_classOfInv, resH2_classOfInv_eq_zero, classOfInv_bijective,
-- exists_resH2_classOfInv_eq, card_kummer_cocycles, finite_Z1_local,
-- IsLocalArtin.exists_frob_of_isUniformiser,
-- char_eq_zero_of_cyclicClass_eq_zero, isTotallyPositive_of_isTotallyComplex,
-- exists_isComplexConj, IsComplexConj.mul_self,
-- IsTotallyPositive.exists_resH2_cyclicClass_eq_zero,
-- IsComplexConj.false_of_isTotallyComplex, IsComplexConj.cycCharMod_eq_neg_one,
-- IsComplexConj.cycChar_eq_neg_one). Part of: "Local class field theory:
-- invariant of the Brauer group, Artin map, norms, tame symbol" and
-- "Local Tate duality in degree 1, as an upper bound for orthogonal groups
-- of cocycles".
-- Encoding. Local fields are IsLocalGalois(G, X, ρ, E, A) of
-- GRH.ClassField.Galois; H²(Γ, Ωˣ) is unitsH2, classOfInv "the unique"
-- class-of-invariant map, and their laws are stated here. The restriction
-- to an open V is read against the local field fixed by V with the
-- restricted action. n·r in ℚ/ℤ is groupPow(qzGroup, r, n).
-- Not stated: pairMapH2_classOfInv (functoriality along j : Ω → Ω′ with
-- ramification e and residue degree f), card_mul_card_le_of_orthogonal,
-- DiscreteModule.HoldsCorestrictions.pairingAnnihilator_le,
-- DiscreteModule.local_duality_card_dvd (the local duality inequality,
-- through corestrictions and FiniteKilledFixedInj), isReal_comp_algebraMap,
-- and LocalDuality/CrystallineDuality.lean (potentially crystalline
-- lattices, which need Lib/PadicHodge).
-- Part of the GRH blueprint (layer 4, Lib/ClassField, stage S1).
-- Copyright (c) 2026 Grant Passmore.
